  "usage_note": "**Rarely** has a negative meaning, so it is not used with **not**: *I rarely go*, not *I don't rarely go*. It usually comes before the main verb or after **be**. At the start of a sentence, mostly in writing, it puts a helping verb before the subject: *Rarely have I seen such a crowd*. **Seldom** means the same but is more formal.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "I don't rarely go there.",
      "correct": "I rarely go there.",
      "note": "**Rarely** is already negative in meaning; do not add **not**."
    }
